# Completion evidence artifacts are content-addressed: the filename IS the
# SHA-256 of the bytes, and a signed evidence record commits to both that hash
# and the exact byte length.
#
# This repository has core.autocrlf=true, so without `-text` git would normalise
# line endings on commit and convert them back on checkout. The bytes on disk
# would then differ per platform — LF on a Linux runner, CRLF on Windows — and
# the artifact would no longer hash to its own filename. The reconciliation test
# would fail on one platform or the other, and worse, the signed record would be
# unverifiable through no fault of the signer.
#
# These files must round-trip byte-for-byte on every platform. Never remove this.
docs/qa/completion/artifacts/** -text
docs/qa/completion-m05/artifacts/** -text
